# GRIP FIGHTING

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

Grip Fighting is a partner-based combat drill designed to develop grip acquisition, grip breaking, hand fighting, tactile awareness and positional dominance before offensive engagement.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-value preparatory combat skills for grappling-based disciplines.

---

# Philosophy

The first battle is often won before the throw, takedown or submission.

It begins with hand control.

Grip Fighting develops the ability to establish dominant grips while denying the opponent the same opportunity.

CAS selects this drill whenever positional superiority is a performance objective.

